# L §2.3 parse rule 3: "A word right after `.` is a field, never a keyword"; L §2.4 Expressions (tally 2.1.4-1): "none
# before a call's `(`, its prefixes and a band's key included". Issue #84 (tally 2.1.5), the M0 builder's finding at
# G8 step 3 (the format fuzz target): a prefixed call whose name is a keyword word printed with a space, `mi.or (DUK)`
# and `mi.and (DUK)`, a text no parser reads back; `canon.spaced` tested for a keyword before the parser's name mark.
# The input is the engine's own test for #84 (format_cases.rs, build/m0 08b7e07), so the canonical text is the same
# bytes in both. Its canonical text reprints as itself (the second file).
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def other: money DUK = round(gross,mi.and(DUK),half-up)

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

input gross: money DUK

def contrib: money DUK = round(gross, mi.or(DUK), half-up)

def inner: money DUK = gross+mi.in(gross)
=== n.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

input gross: money DUK

def contrib: money DUK = round(gross, mi.or(DUK), half-up)

def inner: money DUK = gross + mi.in(gross)

def other: money DUK = round(gross, mi.and(DUK), half-up)
